        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Section 9.3 - Sick Leave",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                461,
                416,
                490
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    134.0,
                    461.0
                ],
                [
                    416.0,
                    461.0
                ],
                [
                    416.0,
                    490.0
                ],
                [
                    134.0,
                    490.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Employee’s shall earn and be granted sick leave, or advanced sick leave in accordance with applicable law, rule, and regulation. Employees must receive approval for sick leave to be granted.",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                517,
                1075,
                603
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    133.0,
                    517.0
                ],
                [
                    1075.0,
                    517.0
                ],
                [
                    1075.0,
                    603.0
                ],
                [
                    133.0,
                    603.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. A Supervisor may require a medical certificate to support use of sick leave for three days or more. An Employee's signed statement certifying that the period of absence is chargeable to sick leave may be accepted when it is unreasonable to require a medical certificate. Circumstances under which an Employee's signed statement is acceptable in lieu of a medical certificate are:",
            "block_bbox": [
                131,
                628,
                1087,
                771
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    131.0,
                    628.0
                ],
                [
                    1087.0,
                    628.0
                ],
                [
                    1087.0,
                    771.0
                ],
                [
                    131.0,
                    771.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a. Inability to secure an appointment with a medical professional during the period of incapacitation.",
            "block_bbox": [
                131,
                796,
                1062,
                852
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    131.0,
                    796.0
